  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Bring 1L (4 cups) water to the boil in a medium saucepan for the noodles. Thickly slice the pak choy stems, leaving the leaves whole. Pick the coriander leaves, discarding the stems. Halve the tofu pieces on an angle.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/801489/photos/large/71059_1-69828cf454ffa9ff7e6321ecf3010560.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Warm tofu: Heat a drizzle of vegetable oil in a small frypan over medium heat. Cook the tofu for 2 mins each side or until slightly charred. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/801490/photos/large/71059_2-2c818141eab5896697ccda06a877734e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook noodles: Meanwhile, cook the noodles in the pan of boiling water for 5 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/801491/photos/large/71059_3-15e18188fad2cb1752f69cd568848c7c.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add pak choy: Add the pak choy, pho seasoning and 1 tsp soy sauce to the noodles. Bring to the boil and cook for 2 mins or until the noodles and pak choy are tender. Remove the pan from the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/801492/photos/large/71059_4-5f09f108bcffb41754fbe1c91f29d049.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the noodles, pak choy and soup among bowls. Top with the tofu, coriander leaves and fried shallots and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/801493/photos/large/71059_5-34d7ef212956a61ce4bb8cd65e334a5b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it spicy: Chilli lovers, go wild and scatter over chopped bird's eyes to serve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/801494/photos/large/71059_6-647014b741ef38bc049607382052687f.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
